.TH SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_HIDAPI_STEAM_HOME_LED 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_HIDAPI_STEAM_HOME_LED \- A variable controlling whether the Steam button LED should be turned on when a Steam controller is opened.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_HIDAPI_STEAM_HOME_LED \(dqSDL_JOYSTICK_HIDAPI_STEAM_HOME_LED\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: Steam button LED is turned off\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: Steam button LED is turned on\[char46]
.PP
By default the Steam button LED state is not changed\[char46] This hint can also be set to a floating point value between 0\[char46]0 and 1\[char46]0 which controls the brightness of the Steam button LED\[char46]
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

